1v (5c, pre-hand-off fixes): all four executed (1g, 1b, 1f, 1p).

## 2 New problems introduced

2a Confirmed requirement changed without marking: none found. The four restorations (R-7, R-29, R-34, R-38) are each flagged in section 10, and R-34.e(2) explicitly fences what it does not test (GP-1).

2b Open question that now leans: none; recommendations were de-leaned (OD-6.d, OD-9.d, OD-14.d, OD-15.d, OD-17.d).

2c Decision the operator has not made: none pre-made, but two labelling inconsistencies are new: 3.3.1.g calls SENT..REPLIED "the confirmed spine" while the glossary Stage entry marks SENT, REPLIED and failure stages [P]; and R-36.e's reflection-record clause plus R-30.e's "collector's reading" are untagged and absent from section 10 despite 6.1.h's promise.

## 3 Verdict

3a Yes, with named small fixes — v0.2 is fit as input for the operator interview and then the threat modeler.

3b Fix 1: align 3.3.1.g with the glossary's authority levels for Stage.

3c Fix 2: tag the R-36.e clause [P] and list it and R-30.e's reading in section 10.

3d Fix 3: replace R-38.d's "review" with the test-reader verification its criterion now describes.
